  "resultText": "`GET /front-desk/queue/metrics` now returns today's average and maximum waiting time. `npm test` passes (36 unit and 5 e2e tests), as do `npm run check:arch`, `typecheck` and `lint`.\n\n**Context map change (needs your sign-off).** Front-desk can't know when an encounter starts, because that belongs to clinical. So I added a clinical → front-desk relation in `context-map.json` (`front-desk.upstream` is now `[\"scheduling\", \"clinical\"]`). Clinical publishes a new `EncounterStarted` event in `src/contracts/clinical.events.ts`. It carries only `appointmentId` and `startedAt`, and front-desk listens for it. This makes front-desk and clinical upstream of each other at the context level. The arch gate allows it because there are no file-level cycles.\n\n**Response**\n```json\n{ \"count\": 2, \"averageWaitingSeconds\": 1200, \"maxWaitingSeconds\": 1800 }\n```\nThe two waiting values are `null` when `count` is 0.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Clinical:** `EncountersService.start` now emits `EncounterStarted`.\n- **Front-desk model:** `Visit` gets a `consultationStartedAt` field and a `waitingTimeMs` getter, set by a new `ClinicalEventsListener`. A new `WaitingTimeMetrics` class computes the average and maximum.\n- **Database:** `FrontDeskVisit.consultationStartedAt` is a new nullable column, so the database needs `npm run db:push`.\n- **Tests:** I added unit tests for `Visit`, `WaitingTimeMetrics`, `VisitsService` and `EncountersService`, plus an e2e test in `test/clinic-flow.e2e-spec.ts`.\n\n**Behaviours to know about**\n- \"Today\" is the UTC calendar day of the check-in. The code has no clinic timezone, so say if you want a different one.\n- Only visitors whose encounter has already started count. Visitors still waiting are left out.\n- Visitors whose encounter has started still appear in `GET /front-desk/queue`, as before. I didn't change the queue.",
